      "writtenOn": "2024-01-12T14:55:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thank you for your comments.\n\nRegarding your first comment, can you please explain more your concerns with this logic and the relation this has to the internal keyboard? The purpose of this is to allow the user to enable a setting and when it is enabled, the keys added to config_additionalWakeKeys will always wake up the device (except for if there is some logic in interceptKeyBeforeQueueing that will disregard the wake key). The idea is that OEMs can add hardware keys such as camera, volume up/down or any other HW key to the array so the user can wake up the display when the power key is unavailable.\n\nRegarding the second comment, I have moved the logic up to where isWakeKey is defined.",
      "parentUuid": "595b75d2_753509f2",
      "revId": "0241d9f067cb73810021182f3da3a9445053a7f9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c4dcd4b1_1693ab74",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/policy/PhoneWindowManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 4594,
      "author": {
        "id": 1950315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-15T13:15:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could you provide some more context about the use cases? I recall reading one about waking the device when it is placed in a case that prevents access to the power button, but in that case it would be better to restrict it to internal keyboards; in a way, a setting to just make all internal keyboard keys a wake key would be more clear, right?",
      "parentUuid": "72826199_cac007ed",
      "revId": "0241d9f067cb73810021182f3da3a9445053a7f9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "51c197ca_ce97998c",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/policy/PhoneWindowManager.java",
