        "id": 1407716
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-16T17:19:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For internal keys, we can define additional wake keys by adding the `WAKE` flag to the KL file for that device ([example](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/base/data/keyboards/Vendor_0957_Product_0001.kl;l\u003d19;drc\u003db4d4b1f22fa7c72764c3b89eaba302a9c02bc1cc)). The difference is that this can\u0027t be enabled/disabled via a setting, but rather is fixed in the build. Is that approach acceptable for your use case?",
      "parentUuid": "c4dcd4b1_1693ab74",
      "revId": "0241d9f067cb73810021182f3da3a9445053a7f9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "49244215_6f95bc4e",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/policy/PhoneWindowManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 4594,
      "author": {
        "id": 1815205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-17T08:50:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We do want the user to be able to enable/disable this via a setting.\n\n\u003e in a way, a setting to just make all internal keyboard keys a wake key would be more clear, right?\n\nYes, I think this would be preferable.\n\nThe question is if there is a way to do what while also being able to enable/disable it with a setting?",
      "parentUuid": "51c197ca_ce97998c",
      "revId": "0241d9f067cb73810021182f3da3a9445053a7f9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
